tional reject for that path (forward_lanb), making a functional gap unlikely.\",\"A minor temporary test artifact (/tmp/nc5432.log) remained on node3 in the final snapshot; this is inconsequential residue from bounded testing, not a persistent misconfiguration.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1-allow","requirement":"node2 (lan-a) can reach node3 (lan-b) on TCP port 5432","status":"satisfied","summary":"Functional TCP connection from node2 to node3:5432 succeeds both before (cmd-4d21ad67dd6845f7, exit=0) and after all three nodes were rebooted (cmd-8276ea6d9bd14b4d, allowed_exit=0). Firewall config (UCI rule + nft dump) confirms only tcp/5432 is accepted lana->lanb.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4d21ad67dd6845f7","cmd-8276ea6d9bd14b4d","cmd-8509d95f06a143b3","cmd-17cc9f2bd37847ed","cmd-71e0124cc3e940fc"]},{"id":"req-2-refuse-forward-other","requirement":"All other node2->node3 traffic (other ports, ICMP) is refused","status":"satisfied","summary":"ICMP ping and TCP to ports 9999/6000 from node2 to node3 fail both pre-restart (cmd-c5412974f8374d80, cmd-ec44195dbfb8415c) and post-restart (cmd-8276ea6d9bd14b4d, other_port_exit=1, ping_exit=1). nft ruleset shows forward_lana only accepts tcp/5432 and rejects everything else.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c5412974f8374d80","cmd-ec44195dbfb8415c","cmd-8276ea6d9bd14b4d","cmd-17cc9f2bd37847ed"]},{"id":"req-3-refuse-reverse","requirement":"All node3->node2 traffic, including TCP 5432, is refused (reverse direction)","status":"satisfied","summary":"TCP connection attempt from node3 to node2:5432 fails both pre- (cmd-bdacfeb38f974f71) and post-restart (cmd-d42c6972ccec47fc). nft dump shows forward_lanb chain unconditionally rejects (jump reject_to_lanb with no exceptions), directly implementing full-reverse-direction refusal; only TCP 5432 in reverse was explicitly probed, not other ports/ICMP in that direction, but the config is unconditional so risk of a gap is low.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bdacfeb38f974f71","cmd-d42c6972cc